  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "J.Thavamani Kumar vs The Food Safety Officer on 11 December, 2024 Author: N.Anand Venkatesh Bench: N.Anand Venkatesh Crl.O.P.(MD)No. Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 11.12.2024 Coram The Hon'Ble Mr.Justice N.Anand Venkatesh Crl.O.P.(MD) No.18261 of 2022 and Crl.M.P.(MD) No.12187 of 2022 J.Thavamani Kumar ... Pet Vs. The Food Safety Officer, Alanganallur Union Registration No.108, Food Safety and Drug Administration, Office of the Designated Officer, Health and Family Welfare Training Centre Campus, Vishwanathapuram 625 503, Madurai District. ...",
    "facts": "This petition has been filed to quash the proceedings pending in STC.No.13 of 2022 on the file of the learned Judicial Magistrate, Vadipatti, Madurai District. 2.The respondent has filed a private complaint against the petitioner for offence under Sections 51, 58 and 59(i) of the 'Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006' (hereinafter referred to as 'the Act' for brevity). The allegation made in the complaint is that on 13.05.2020 at about 11.15 a.m., an inspection was conducted by the Food Safety Officer in the shop belonging to the petitioner and gingelly oil in loose condition was drawn as a sample in four packets. Thereafter, it was sent for test to the food analyst on 14.05.2020 which was received on 18.05.2020 and the report dated 30.07.2020 was issued stating that the sample is sub- standard and unsafe and prohibitions and restrictions on sales. On receipt of the report, the designated officer sent his recommendation on 10.08.2020 to the Commissioner for initiation of prosecution. On receipt of the sanction, the private complaint came to be filed before the Court https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Crl.O.P.(MD)No.18261 of 2022 below.",
    "arguments": "4.Apart from other grounds that were raised by the learned counsel for the petitioner, the main ground that was raised was that the petitioner was denied an opportunity of sending the sample for further test as provided under Section 46(4) of the Act.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4.Apart from other grounds that were raised by the learned counsel for the petitioner, the main ground that was raised was that the petitioner was denied an opportunity of sending the sample for further test as provided under Section 46(4) of the Act.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
